# Frontend rules

## Structure

- Features: `src/features/<domain>/{components,hooks,utils,types,constants,api,pages}`
- Design system: `src/ui/{atoms,molecules,organisms,templates}` — **no domain knowledge**
- Routing: `src/routes.ts` (RouteConfig) + thin modules in `src/routes/`
- Root: `src/root.tsx` (Layout, Outlet, ErrorBoundary, HydrateFallback)
- Providers: `src/app/providers/`
- Shared: `src/shared/` (`invoke`, `cn`, shared types)
- i18n: `src/i18n/{en,es,de}.json` — no hard-coded user-facing strings

## Routing (React Router 7 Framework Mode)

- Define routes only in `src/routes.ts` using `index`, `route`, `layout`, `prefix` from `@react-router/dev/routes`.
- Follow https://reactrouter.com/start/framework/routing
- Do **not** use `createBrowserRouter`, `createHashRouter`, or `RouterProvider` for primary navigation.
- Route modules stay thin; render `features/*/pages` components.
- SPA: `react-router.config.ts` has `ssr: false`. Prefer `clientLoader` / `clientAction` for data.

## Atomic Design

`pages → templates → organisms → molecules → atoms` (never import upward).
`ui` never imports `features`. Features import `@/ui`, never `@radix-ui/*`.

## Thin pages (mandatory)

Pages are **composition only**. Reading a page file should tell you the screen storyboard at a glance (`PageHeader`, filters, table, pagination) — not a wall of labels, inputs, and layout `div`s.

- **Do not** paste repeated chrome inline: page title/subtitle blocks, search+filter toolbars, pagination, loading/error status, labeled field rows, button-styled links.
- **Do** extract to:
  - `src/ui/*` when reusable across domains (`Page`, `PageHeader`, `SearchField`, `CheckboxField`, `PaginationBar`, `LinkButton`, `DefinitionList`, `StatusMessage`)
  - `features/<domain>/components/` when domain-specific (`CustomerListFilters`, `CustomerDetailFields`)
- Prefer meaningful names over generic wrappers (`CustomerListFilters`, not `FiltersBox`).
- If the same markup appears twice (or will appear on the next domain page), extract it **now**.

## State logic

- Components stay thin.
- Hooks own state, effects, TanStack Form instances, TanStack Table instances.
- Utils are pure (no React, no `invoke`).
- Pages do not call `invoke` directly — go through feature `api` + hooks.

## Mandatory libraries

- **Forms:** `@tanstack/react-form` for every create/edit form
- **Tables:** `@tanstack/react-table` for every data table; prefer SQL pagination from Rust
- **Styling:** Tailwind v4 + `styles/tokens.css`; prefer semantic token classes (`bg-primary`)
- Do not use React Hook Form, Formik, or MUI/Ant as substitutes

## Performance

Quiet visuals; limited blur/shadow/animation. Add Radix packages only when needed.
